s policy.<br><br><strong>Information Technology (IT) Department / Network Team:</strong> Responsible for the secure design, implementation, maintenance, and monitoring of all authorized wireless infrastructure. This includes managing the WIDS/WIPS, applying patches, and responding to incidents.<br><br><strong>Information Security Team:</strong> Responsible for policy review, conducting security assessments, analyzing WIDS/WIPS alerts, and investigating policy violations.<br><br><strong>All Users:</strong> Required to comply with all aspects of this policy, use only authorized wireless networks for business, and report any suspected security incidents or unauthorized wireless devices immediately.</p>\"",\""defaultEnabled\"":true},{\""title\"":\""Enforcement\"",\""content\"":\""<p>Compliance with this policy will be enforced through a combination of technical controls, automated monitoring, and administrative procedures. Violations of this policy may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment or contractual agreement, and may lead to civil or criminal liability. The IT Department is authorized to immediately disconnect any unauthorized wireless device or network posing a security risk. All users shall be required to formally acknowledge receipt and understanding of this policy upon hire and annually thereafter.</p>\"",\""defaultEnabled\"":true},{\""title\"":\""Review and Revision\"",\""content\"":\""<p>This Wireless Security Policy shall be reviewed by the Information Security team at least annually, or more frequently in response to significant security incidents, changes in threat landscape, or updates to relevant standards (ISO 27001, NIST, etc.). Proposed revisions must be submitted to the CISO for approval. The latest approved version of this policy shall be made accessible to all personnel through the corporate policy repository.</p>\"",\""defaultEnabled\"":true}]""",2025-12-20 21:17:22.821891,"""[\""ISO 27001\"",\""SOC 2\""]"""